    fix(agent-loop): preserve prompt history during supported tool updates
    
    Tool changes previously forced prompt consolidation even when the prepared
    route could activate new tools through history. Rewriting the first system
    message, or clearing an earlier appended prompt, reset the declaration
    series and turned additions into immediate declarations.
    
    Only routes without toolUpdate need that tool-triggered consolidation.
    Capable routes append the full changed prompt and keep existing messages.
    Explicit series starts, surface replacements, and unsupported prompt
    routes still consolidate; retained-name definition changes still rebuild
    tool declarations in Session.
    
    Cover both update modes and reset paths, and pin the combined prompt/tool
    transition through the shipped headless profile with shared schema goldens.

